## Flight Report

**Left gate:** Crossed at decision k=9 (the 2.5 m straight move from the lined-up pose at x≈-0.06, y≈0.05, heading +21°). The k=10 view confirmed a clean transit — the filmstrip showed both posts splitting symmetrically to the frame edges and vanishing, with the crossbar passing overhead in the downward camera. This crossing was through the middle, after a lengthy lineup that included two overshoot/back-up cycles (R5) before settling on heading +21°.

**Center gate:** Not found or crossed. After clearing the left gate's post zone (k=10) and moving toward the strategy's expected "ahead-right, deeper +x, toward -y" vicinity (k=11–12), the forward camera only ever showed a table, a mannequin figure, and wall shelving — no yellow posts or teal crossbar at any point, including after two scanning turns (k=12, k=13). I ran out of decisions (14 total) before locating it.

**Penguin:** Never located in either camera.

**Final pose:** x=4.50, y=-0.12, z=1.50, heading=-46° (approx, after the last unlogged +yaw -20 turn from -26°).

**Overall:** Incomplete. Only the left gate was crossed cleanly through the middle; the center gate and penguin hover were not achieved. The lineup on the left gate consumed more decisions than budgeted (9 of 14) due to repeated "one post close" overshoots, leaving too few decisions to locate and cross the center gate afterward.
